{"name":"Banana Boat","hex":"#fdc838","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"banana boat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inflatable recreational boat meant for towing, often yellow and banana-shaped.","A ship designed to transport bananas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banana_boat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Consolidated B-24 Liberator","blocks":[{"text":"The Consolidated B-24 Liberator is an American heavy bomber, designed by Consolidated Aircraft of San Diego, California. It was known within the company as the Model 32, and some initial production aircraft were laid down as export models designated as various LB-30s, in the Land Bomber design category."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Maxwell_B-24_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Maxwell_B-24_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consolidated_B-24_Liberator"},{"title":"RAF slang","blocks":[{"text":"The Royal Air Force (RAF) developed a distinctive slang which has been documented in works such as Piece of Cake and the Dictionary of RAF slang."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/A_party_of_riggers_working_on_the_tailplane_of_a_Supermarine_Spitfire_of_No._601_Squadron_at_Lentini_West%2C_Sicily%2C_7_September_1943._CNA1329.jpg/330px-A_party_of_riggers_working_on_the_tailplane_of_a_Supermarine_Spitfire_of_No._601_Squadron_at_Lentini_West%2C_Sicily%2C_7_September_1943._CNA1329.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RAF_slang"},{"title":"Banana Boat","blocks":[{"text":"Banana Boat is a Polish a cappella sextet, authoring and performing original songs representing the genre of neo-shanties. Being one of the pioneers of the new genre, the group retains its simultaneous focus on contemporary interpretations of traditional sea shanties and maritime music. Owing to its characteristic six-part, jazzy harmony, departing from the traditional sound of the music of the sea, the group has become one of the emblems of what the international artists of the maritime stage have informally come to dub as the Polish style maritime song. With maritime music constantly in the focus of its activity, since 2004, Banana Boat has also been experimenting with other musical genres, including popular and jazz compositions, inviting other artists to participate in individual projects. The group is a member of the International Seasong and Shanty Association (ISSA)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Bananaboat.jpg/330px-Bananaboat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana_Boat"},{"title":"Banana boat (ship)","blocks":[{"text":"Banana boat is a descriptive nickname that was given to fast ships, also called banana carriers, engaged in the banana trade. They were designed to transport easily spoiled bananas rapidly from tropical growing areas to North America and Europe. They often carried passengers as well as fruit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/USS_Merak_%28AF-21%29_underway_at_sea%2C_23_June_1943.jpg/330px-USS_Merak_%28AF-21%29_underway_at_sea%2C_23_June_1943.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana_boat_(ship)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/XB-24_in_Flight.jpg/500px-XB-24_in_Flight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/XB-24_in_Flight.jpg/1280px-XB-24_in_Flight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/XB-24_in_Flight.jpg/500px-XB-24_in_Flight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c